    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serving as the clear offensive anchor. His elite projection of 80.98 is the only score eclipsing the 60-threshold, driven by an optimal matchup against Feltner. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from a massive 14% park boost and a high-leverage leadoff spot, making him our primary engine for both runs and the scarcity-driven SB category. While the rest of the lineup sits in the marginal-to-strong \"high-40s to mid-50s\" range, **Chase Meidroth** (58.15) and **Colt Keith** (57.27) provide steady production. **Chase Meidroth** is currently capitalizing on a favorable SP_xERA of 4.41 and the platoon advantage hitting at the top of the order, while **Colt Keith** gains significant efficiency from a soft matchup against Matthews, where his ability to exploit a slow delivery profile adds a critical 2% premium to his SB ceiling.\n\nThe most challenging decision today involved the bottom of the utility slot, where **Lars Nootbaar** (53.91) narrowly edged out internal depth candidates. **Lars Nootbaar** was favored largely due to an 11% dynamic platoon boost and a strong xwOBA profile of .373 against Scott, which provides a higher floor than our typical bench depth. We are monitoring **Luke Raley** (54.59) closely, as he remains a strong start in a hitter-friendly park; however, he carries a 42% rain risk that could compromise his plate appearances or lead to a shortened game. With core studs like **Yordan Alvarez**, **Junior Caminero**, **Trea Turner**, and **Kyle Schwarber** sidelined by team off-days, our bench remains thin, necessitating that **Dillon Dingler** (44.13) and **Carson Benge** (56.54) produce despite the latter\u2019s slight negative park adjustment. We continue to track the availability of **Christian Yelich**, **Caleb Durbin**, **Hyeseong Kim**, **Rece Hinds**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Zac Veen**, **Nelson Velazquez**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Josh Smith**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Luis Pena**, **Jose Fernandez**, and **Pedro Ramirez** to ensure our roster depth remains optimized for the scarcity of SBs moving forward.",
